/-!
# Proper simple sections of the alternating quasithin models

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, Theorem 0.1.2(3), condition K, printed pp.4 and 482.
The intended conclusion covers every simple quotient of every subgroup of
each proper subgroup of A₅, A₆, A₈ and A₉, using actual carrier equivalences.

The A₅ and A₆ clauses are proved in `SmallDegrees`: their proper simple
sections are prime cyclic and prime cyclic or A₅, respectively. The
degree-eight and degree-nine section classifications and their final assembly
remain open. The K-class inclusion is left explicit for the full-catalogue
assembly; the partial constructed catalogue is not identified with source K.
-/
